package card

// Section is one labelled block inside a Card. Renders a heading
// (`title`) + optional subtitle on top, then the templ children
// underneath as the body. When two or more Sections sit as direct
// siblings inside the same Card, the second-and-later ones automatically
// gain a `pt-4 border-t border-kiban-border` divider, producing the
// stacked-with-rules layout used on form pages and detail screens.
//
// The auto-divider relies on Tailwind's `first:` modifier: the first
// `card.Section` rendered inside a parent gets `pt-0` + `border-t-0`,
// the rest get the divider classes. If non-Section content (e.g. a
// flash banner) is rendered before the first Section, the first Section
// will incorrectly pick up a top border — keep flash banners outside
// the Card or use a single-Section layout in that case.
//
// Body spacing inside a Section is `space-y-5`, matching the form rhythm
// already used by the rekon backoffice forms; if you need a different
// rhythm wrap your children in a div with the spacing you want.
templ Section(title, subtitle string) {
	<div class="space-y-5 pt-4 border-t border-kiban-border first:pt-0 first:border-t-0">
		<div class="space-y-1">
			<div class="font-heading font-medium text-base text-kiban-ink">{ title }</div>
			if subtitle != "" {
				<div class="text-sm text-kiban-ink3">{ subtitle }</div>
			}
		</div>
		{ children... }
	</div>
}
